    "note": "Senate Draft 2. Effective 1/1/2026. Section 2 is a standalone grandfather clause, not an amendment of HRS 134-8 text. The first sentence of subsection (c) (ten-round pistol limit) is existing law with word edits and is not quoted. Amendments made after the version read are not in the text read."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (HRS 134-8): The manufacture, possession, sale, barter, trade, gift, transfer, or acquisition of any detachable ammunition magazine with a capacity in excess of thirty rounds that is designed for or capable of use with any firearm other than a pistol is prohibited.\nSECTION 2 (HRS 134-8): This Act shall not prohibit possession of a detachable ammunition magazine with a capacity in excess of thirty rounds that is designed for or capable of use with any firearm other than a pistol that was legally obtained prior to the effective date of this Act."
